
# Napa shoot masters, dropped into assets/journal/ 2026-08-29 — 570 files, 354MB.
# The masters do not belong in the repo; only the webp derivatives this build
# actually serves do. This is the same fault as the three MP4s that permanently
# block a whole-tree push, caught before it was committed rather than after.
assets/journal/*.jpg
assets/journal/*.jpeg
assets/journal/*.JPG

# ── raw shoot masters, untracked 2026-09-03 ───────────────────────
# 57.6MB across 59 files that no page, stylesheet or script references:
# 34 camera masters dropped into assets/logos/ beside the real brand PNGs,
# 16 numbered originals at the assets/ root, the FAQ chairs photograph the
# owner removed from the homepage, and a few leftover seams.
#
# Listed exactly rather than by pattern. `assets/pool-*.webp` was tried and
# would have caught pool-121212 and four siblings that ARE on the page —
# every brand logo is a .png and every one of them survives this list.
#
# Deleted from disk 2026-09-03, after checking each one three ways: present
# in the repo, byte-identical copy in ../reptify-media-2026.subtree-backup,
# and referenced by no HTML, CSS, JS, JSON, XML or txt in the tree. The list
# stays here so a re-import of the same masters is ignored rather than
# silently re-added. Recovery, if ever needed, is the subtree backup.
